  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "other",
      "components": ["U9"],
      "pins": ["U9.1"],
      "nets": ["+3.3V", "NET0128", "NET0096"],
      "observed": "On the FCC Peripherals sheet, the PCA9685PW (U9) address pin A0 (pin 1) is strapped to +3.3V while A1–A5 (pins 3, 4, 5, 24) and OE (pin 25) go to GND, and the sheet's own note reads 'I2C address: 0x41'. The device sits on the same I2C bus as the INA219 (SCL=NET0128, SDA=NET0096, INA219 at 0x40) and the FCC EEPROM (0x50).",
      "expected": "The specification's component table states the PWM/servo driver is 'NXP PCA9685PW (I2C 16-ch PWM), I2C addr 0x40', i.e. all address pins strapped low. The as-drawn strapping (A0 high) moves the device to 0x41, deviating from the intended address.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "PWM/servo driver | FCCPeripherals | NXP PCA9685PW (I2C 16-ch PWM), I2C addr 0x40 | FCCPeripherals.sch note \"PWM Driver\""},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "FCC Peripherals sheet: U9 PCA9685PW, pin 1 A0 tied to +3.3V, note 'I2C address: 0x41'"}
      ],
      "impact": "Firmware built against the reference design (PCA9685 at 0x40) will not acknowledge the PWM driver at this address, so no servo PWM outputs are generated; alternatively, if the board is treated as the reference, the servo channel bank is effectively dead.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most of the schematic matches the specification (dual STM32H753/STM32F405 MCUs, sensor set and addresses, 10 mΩ shunt with INA219 at 0x40, 15 µH buck with 6.8k/1.3k divider giving ~5 V, 3.3 V LDO, 25 MHz crystals, CH330 bridges, and the documented barometer RESET/EOC mix-up bug). The one deviation the drawing supports is the PCA9685 PWM driver being strapped to I2C address 0x41 (A0 tied high) instead of the specified 0x40, which would leave the servo driver unreachable at the address the intended firmware expects."
}

